-- Test Description
-- This test introduces long periods of DMA bus activity, by stopping hready,
-- such that it causes overflows on receive.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage  																																																																											  tion.
-- * Checks the overflow indication of the RX MAC
-- * Checks the overflow indication of the FIFO
-- * Checks the detection of overflow on EOP writes
-- * Checks the detection of overflow on SOP writes
-- * Checks DMA buffer recovery after detection of overflow
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
-- 1. Setup DMA wait states for the test.
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for 100Mbits/s 32-bit DMA mode.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts, and then enable receive.
-- 4. Receive a frame that is 256 bytes long. Stop hready near the end of 
--    the frame such that the receive FIFO overflows on the final write.
--    Check that an overflow status is indicated and that the next frame
--    recovers the current buffer.
-- 5. Receive a frame that is 256 bytes long. Ensure that hready is still
--    stopped from the end of the last test such that overflow is still
--    indicated when about to do the SOP write.
--    Check that an overflow status is indicated and that no DMA activity
--    is seen. Check that the next frame recovers the same buffer
-- 6. Receive a frame that is 256 bytes long. Stop hready near the end of the
--    first buffer such that the receive FIFO overflows momentarily.
--    Check that an overflow status is generated and that the final buffer
--    is recovered.
-- 7. Receive a good frame of 64 bytes.
-- 8. check statistic registers
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


-- *****************************************************************************
-- 1. Setup DMA wait states for the test.
-- *****************************************************************************
